      "body": "The repo's own config reports five E704 that cannot be fixed from the source side:\n\n```\n$ python -m flake8 --config=.flake8 --select=E,W,F torchtitan\ntorchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/graph_pp/stage_builder.py:59:5: E704 multiple statements on one line (def)\n...  (5 in that file)\n```\n\nAll five are ellipsis-only stub bodies written as `def f(...) -> T: ...`. That form is what the project formatter emits:\n\n```\n$ ruff format --diff torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/graph_pp/stage_builder.py\n1 file already formatted\n```\n\nAnd expanding a stub does not survive formatting — writing the body on its own line makes `ruff format` collapse it straight back:\n\n```\n-    ) -> list[Any]:\n-        ...\n+    ) -> list[Any]: ...\n1 file would be reformatted\n```\n\nSo E704 is a linter/formatter conflict, not a code smell. This adds it to the existing `ignore` list with a comment explaining why, and leaves everything else untouched (`B007,B008` etc. are still reported).\n\n```\nbefore:  python -m flake8 --config=.flake8 --select=E704 torchtitan  -> 5\nafter:   python -m flake8 --config=.flake8 --select=E704 torchtitan  -> 0\n```\n\nAlternative if you would rather not widen the global ignore: a `per-file-ignores` entry for `torchtitan/experiments/*`. Happy to switch.",
